  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (16 witnesses, 23 names, composes nothing), so the node is done and 5 of the 6 gate runs are unused.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_450_1o.lean`):\n- **Applies when** the subject vehicle is in a lane governed by a no_stopping, no_standing or no_parking sign whose conditions hold for it, or is on a no_stopping or no_parking curb zone.\n- **Violated when** the vehicle makes the halt that place forbids and no exception holds:\n  - under no_stopping, any halt;\n  - under no_standing, a halt longer than the standing duration;\n  - under no_parking, a halt longer than the parking duration.\n- **Exceptions:** I put them in the obligation, where the node puts them, so an excused halt counts as compliant rather than out of scope. They are:\n  - another road user ahead in the same lane within the queue gap;\n  - a stop sign, a yield sign, a red signal, or level-crossing lights or gate, governing the vehicle's lane;\n  - a police officer directing the lane to stop.\n- **Overlap in the node:** its \"compliance with law\" exception (stop sign, red signal) is fully contained in its traffic-control-device exception, so I wrote the combined list once. I declared no narrowings of my own.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_450_1o.lean`): the eight planned scenarios have their planned verdicts. I added eight more to cover branches the plan didn't reach:\n- a no_standing sign and a no_stopping curb zone, both violated;\n- one compliant halt for each excusing device (stop sign, yield sign, red signal, railway lights, railway gate, police officer).\n\nBefore the real gate run, I mistakenly tried an extra command (the gate with a `--help` flag). The permission system blocked it, so it didn't run and used no gate budget.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory with these choices and the run log.",
